      ],
      "decision": "Reference frame and relativity of rest; speed magnitude addition restricted to classical codirectional collinear case. No universal same-vs-opposed summation. Egg collision question is underdetermined by motion/rest alone and not keyed."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        4,
        5,
        6,
        7
      ],
      "decision": "Coordinate dimensions/time and sourced s=v*t only. Infinite universe is not an established observed fact. PDF5 printed12 airplane4300-year estimate is about1000 times too small for its given distance/speed; not copied. Historical second-as-year-fraction and universal clock precision statements not assessed; current SI second unit retained."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        7,
        8,
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "decision": "Material point depends on task. Path scalar vs displacement vector; straight-line reversal invalidates general path=displacement-magnitude statement. Historical metre metal-bar definition not presented as current. Translation can be curved without rotation."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        11,
        12,
        13,
        14,
        15,
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "decision": "Vectors need direction; only codirectional collinear lengths add by magnitude. Opposed numerical branch a>=b has result along a, equality zero. Positive scalar k<1 reduces magnitude despite prose 'increases'; negative k reverses direction taught conceptually. Triangle/subtraction/projection diagrams image-checked; no unsupported trig law. PDF17 Earth east-to-west rotation claim is wrong and not copied. Supplement exercises not separate counted lessons; key skills included."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        19,
        20,
        21
      ],
      "decision": "Straightness vs constant speed distinguished; constant speed circle not constant velocity vector. Finite uniform-spaced samples alone do not prove global uniformity. Interval count is gaps, not marks. Repeated equal distances s=d*n derived only for equal intervals; no premature acceleration formula."
    }
  ],
